<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10566" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-sŏnus</span></b> , a, um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj., sounding
				together in harmony, harmonious</i> (rare, mostly <b>poet.</b>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clangor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 13, 610</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fila lyrae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Am. 1, 8, 60</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vox,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					17, 448</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consŏna</span></b> , ae, f., =
			consonans, <i>a consonant</i>, <i><span class="en">Ter.
				Maur. p. 2395</span></i> P. sq.; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consona elementa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. p. 2385</span></i>
			 ib.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>accordant, fit,
				suitable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fila telae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Rapt. Pros. 2, 42</span></i>
			: credo Platonem vix putasse satis consonum fore, si, etc.,
			* <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 4, 16, 3</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 114</span></i>. —With
				<i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consona regno juvenem docere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Laud. Stil. 2, 69</span></i>
			.—* <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-sŏnē</span></b> ,
				<i>harmoniously</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clamitare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 1, p. 106, 34</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
